## Corrections Log — read before deciding

[`docs/corrections-log.md`](docs/corrections-log.md) records every time an agent was wrong
on this project and every time a decision had to be pushed back. Read its **Patterns**
section before acting. The ledger is the evidence behind it. The checks that apply to
every agent, at every step
([`RULES.md#evidence-corrections--decisions`](.opencode/skills/RULES.md#evidence-corrections--decisions)):

1. Before writing *already done / out of scope / resolved / pre-existing*, run the
   command that proves it and cite the output. Narrowing scope is the product owner's
   call.
2. Before keeping a test, break what it guards and watch it fail. Break every line that
   enforces the control.
3. Before claiming a document was amended, `git diff` the passage.
4. Before reporting a result, quote the failures too.
5. Brief reviewers with the original request, the diff, and existing evidence (the local
   CI report or "pending: hosted CI on the PR head", scanner output, and the privacy
   screening), never a list of what was done or where to look.
6. After fixing a write, find every other writer of the same state. When a shared
   function is wrong, fix it at that function, not at the caller that noticed.
7. When a rule, claim or name changes, grep every copy of it (proposal, ADR, PIA, risk
   register, this file, agent and skill files) and make each agree. After removing a
   name, search for it.

This entry is the durable copy: `update-skills` can overwrite the skills' own pointers.
Append an entry to the log when you get something wrong.

