## Testing & Local CI

See [`RULES.md#testing`](.opencode/skills/RULES.md#testing). Plus:

- **CI on pull requests: [yes | no].** Keep the one bullet that applies:
  - *yes:* Where hosted CI runs on pull requests, a review held before the PR exists
    records the CI evidence as **"pending: hosted CI on the PR head"**; the gate is
    re-checked on the PR head before merge: green is required to merge, and the agent
    that opens the PR waits for the run and reports it, failures quoted. A local report
    is not required.
  - *no:* run CI locally before every PR with `[local CI command, e.g. a runner script
    that reads the workflow file]`, against the **committed** branch (pass the commit,
    e.g. `--ref <sha>`, when running from a worktree). Run every CI job the change
    touches, and all of them for a dependency, workflow or config change. The report
    names the jobs that ran and those **SKIPPED**. A SKIPPED job is **NOT VERIFIED**,
    never "passing", and the reviewer blocks a missing or non-compliant report. It is
    the only check before merge; never push to the default branch to find out.

